Project Overview:

style: smashy road (low polygon)-esque very similair graphics


Land:
Isometric view of regular tiles

The tiles form a landscape of coniferous forest and each tile has an associated height making it a hilly/mountainous scene.

Each tile has its own properties and can be in one of three states:

On fire
Burnt (regrows after a certain timestep and neighbouring conditions)
Not on fire

Each tile has associated properties that affect its behaviour as well as an associated height.

Land can be of the default 4 types:
- grass
- forest
- sand
- rocky
- water
The type affects if it can be set on fire and how

Fire:

Fire can spread to neighbouring tiles with a certain probability depending in a few factors:

wind(affects tiles directionally)
fuel (whats on the tiles)
Slope (fire spreads easier up a slope)
-fire severity and pre-existing area of fire

Fire can have different severity affecting how long its going to last for, how much water it needs to be put out with

Fires produce smoke which sits above the fire, dispersing over time once the tile is not on fire, must have multiple tiles for it to be smoky

Drones:



Drones start from a home base and go to collect water from water sources (e.g. river pond reservoir)

When the drones can communicate they make interlinked decisions about how to most effectively as a group extinguish the fire (can define number of drones to start with)

However sometimes they cannot communicate with each other:

-when they are out of range
-when there is smoke between them (treat as infinite distances)
-when there hills between them (treat as infinite distance)

drones have a durability that diminishes over time but can be sped of by different factors such as wind, going up or going down etc

Drones can fly over fire and in smoke, but it means their durability decreases much quicker. if the drones lose all durability they break and are lost for good.

Drones must return to the home base to replenish their durability.

Drones have their own map of where the fire are based on the initial map they get from home-base and also can share them with other drones to inform others on the current situation and how to solve them

When drones are in range of base/ go to recharge, they share their map so that the home base has a more complete map of where the fire is that it can share with drones,

In the case that a drone has a fire map with no fire on it , it goes back to homebase to get the firemaps from them

Drones can share their maps of the fire, the more recent one is taken to be more accurate.
